    <!-- OVERVIEW TABLE -->
    <h2>System Modules Overview</h2>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Module</th>
                <th>Primary Function</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Management Panel</strong></td>
                <td>Full operational control, user roles, and central auditing.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Sales & Engagement</strong></td>
                <td>Lead lifecycle tracking and flat booking management.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>CED & Collection</strong></td>
                <td>Payment receipting, cheque tracking, and accounts bridge.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Finance & Accounts</strong></td>
                <td>Cash flow, double-entry bookkeeping, and vendor payouts.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>HRM & Payroll</strong></td>
                <td>Employee records, attendance, and monthly payroll.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Construction (Ph 2)</strong></td>
                <td>Design, BOQ, procurement, and execution monitoring.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <!-- SECTION 1 -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>1. Executive Overview</h2>
    <p>
        The TPHL-ERP is a custom-built enterprise solution designed to integrate construction project management, financial accounting, human resources, and sales pipelines. It provides secure, role-based access for streamlined oversight.
    </p>

    <h3>1.1 All-Over Management Panel</h3>
    <p>
        Designed for Super Admins and Directors to exercise absolute control over all business segments:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Global Settings:</strong> Manage system configurations, APIs, and maintenance.</li>
        <li><strong>User Registry:</strong> Monitor employee credentials and active session controls.</li>
        <li><strong>Role Configurator:</strong> Define fine-grained permission matrices (CRUD) for all roles.</li>
        <li><strong>Financial Audit:</strong> Company-wide cash-in/out visibility and transaction overrides.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- SECTION 2 -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>2. Sales & Customer Engagement</h2>
    <p>
        The Sales Module manages the client lifecycle, starting from lead acquisition and continuous nurturing, up to flat booking allocations and dynamic installment collection tracking.
    </p>

    <h3>2.1 Panel Roles & Pipeline Overview</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Lead Tracking:</strong> Manage source-based pipelines (Facebook, Referrals, etc.) and follow-up logs.</li>
        <li><strong>Booking Inventory:</strong> Interactive floor plans for flat availability (Booked, Sold, Blocked).</li>
        <li><strong>Payment Scheduling:</strong> Automated EMI generation with unique installment codes and due dates.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>2.2 Key Features & Processing Workflows</h3>
    <h4>Lead Lifecycle Tracking:</h4>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Lead Sources:</strong> Organize incoming leads by source (e.g., Facebook, Google Ads, Referrals, Walk-ins).</li>
        <li><strong>Status Pipelines:</strong> Track leads through standard pipelines (New, Contacted, Visited, Negotiation, Booked, Lost).</li>
        <li><strong>Follow-Up Logs:</strong> Record detailed discussion notes for each interaction and schedule the next follow-up date (which automatically feeds into the Executive's dashboard calendar).</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Flat Booking Management:</h4>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Inventory Selection:</strong> Interactively view flat statuses (Available, Booked, Sold, Blocked) grouped by Project and Floor.</li>
        <li><strong>Booking Form:</strong> Process client personal details, nominee info, agreed price, booking money, downpayment agreements, and total installment count.</li>
        <li><strong>Dynamic Payment Scheduling:</strong> Automatically generate customized installment plans (EMI schedules) with unique installment codes, due dates, and amounts.</li>
    </ul>

    <h4>Onboard Client Portal:</h4>
    <p>
        Convert successfully negotiated leads into active clients. Link personal contact info, flat ownership registers, and custom discount/car-parking values to the client profile.
    </p>

    <!-- SECTION 3 -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>3. Collection & Financial Core</h2>
    <p>
        Ensures financial integrity through specialized collection and bookkeeping modules:
    </p>

    <h3>3.1 Key Features & Workflows</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>CED Dashboard:</strong> Real-time tracking of targets, due installments, and cheque status.</li>
        <li><strong>Money Receipts:</strong> Serialized receipt generation with bank log integration and auto-reconciliation.</li>
        <li><strong>Expense Management & Approvals:</strong> Double-entry ledger for operational funds, vendor bills, and payroll payouts.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- SECTION 4 -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>4. Human Capital Management</h2>
    
    <h3>4.1 HRM Panel Features</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Attendance:</strong> Biometric and Geofenced mobile punch integration with late/absent reporting.</li>
        <li><strong>Payroll Engine:</strong> Single-click payout calculation factoring in allowances, deductions, and loans.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>4.2 Employee Self-Service</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Self-Service Portal:</strong> Employee portal for payslip downloads, leave requests, and task management.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- SECTION 5 -->
    <div class="page-break"></div>
    <h2>5. Construction Phase 2</h2>
    <p>
        Coordinates the full construction lifecycle from land acquisition to QC auditing.
    </p>

    <h3>5.1 Role-Based Construction Panels</h3>
    <table>
        <thead>
            <tr>
                <th>Role</th>
                <th>Primary Access & Core Features</th>
            </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Project Manager Head / Operations Head</strong></td>
                <td>Portfolio overview, approval of BOQ budgets, work orders, contractor bills, monthly review finalizations, and project risk mitigations.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Project Manager (PM)</strong></td>
                <td>Project timeline setups, monthly target planning, weekly calendar approvals, vendor quotation reviews, purchase order finalizations, and site progress audits.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Site Engineer (SE)</strong></td>
                <td>Daily progress logging, material receiving (GRN) verification, material issue vouchers, labor logs, and weekly progress submissions.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>QC Auditor / QC Specialist</strong></td>
                <td>Master checklist setup, site inspections (Passed, Failed, Rework Needed), and material lab test logs.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Architect / Structural Designer</strong></td>
                <td>Project drawing registry (Civil, Architectural, Electrical, Plumbing), soil test documentation, and revision control tracking.</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
                <td><strong>Estimator</strong></td>
                <td>Initial budget estimates, Bill of Quantities (BOQ) planning, and material specification setups.</td>
            </tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>

    <h3>5.2 Key Modules & Operational Workflows</h3>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Procurement:</strong> Handles PR/PO workflows with estimate-based budget limit checks.</li>
        <li><strong>Execution:</strong> Weekly progress logging, measurement sheets, and contractor bill validation.</li>
        <li><strong>Risk Recovery:</strong> Auto-detection of burn-rate delays and missed targets with action item tracking.</li>
    </ul>

</body>
</html>
